{"id":"n-20261025-vzvlim","category":"health","display_title":"10-Hour Ambulance Wait for Elderly Woman","display_title_he":"המתנה של 10 שעות לאמבולנס עבור אישה מבוגרת","short_summary":"A 93-year-old woman in Wales endured a ten-and-a-half-hour wait on her home floor with broken bones before an ambulance arrived. Her son criticized the healthcare system's response times, prompting an official apology and review.","english_level":"C1","words":457,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Mexican_air_ambulance_fleet.jpg/960px-Mexican_air_ambulance_fleet.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Ojuanialakentu · CC BY-SA 4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mexican_air_ambulance_fleet.jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"BBC News","domain":"bbc.co.uk","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm9dzj60z2pqo","title":"My 93-year-old mother waited 10 hours on the floor for an ambulance","published_at":"2026-10-24T20:54:47.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-24T20:54:47.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-25T06:14:48.671Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["A ninety-three-year-old woman in Wales suffered a fractured femur and shoulder during a fall at her home, enduring a ten-and-a-half-hour wait on the floor before an ambulance finally transported her to the hospital. Her son, Graham Anthony, rushed to her property after receiving an automated alert from her lifeline alarm early in the morning. According to his account, he placed the call for an ambulance shortly before eight o'clock, yet professional medical transport did not arrive for many hours. Eventually, a St John Ambulance worker arrived following a request by the Welsh Ambulance Service, and an actual ambulance transported her ninety minutes later.","Margaret Owen, who lives with dementia in Abercynon within Rhondda Cynon Taf, was found in severe distress with her right leg immobilized and complaining of intense arm pain. Because of her dementia, she struggled to remember exactly what happened, and her son noted he did not know how long she lay on the floor before activating the alarm. Although she underwent surgery for her broken bones at Royal Glamorgan Hospital, she remained admitted weeks after the incident. Mr Anthony expressed profound frustration regarding the ordeal, noting that listening to his mother repeatedly ask for assistance and sometimes scream in pain left him feeling utterly hopeless. While he commended the professionalism of the crew who ultimately treated her really well, he admitted that the distressing experience severely undermined his confidence in the health service's ability to respond.","Following a post on a Facebook page detailing the incident, Mr Anthony received an enormous response from hundreds of individuals sharing similar tales of delayed care for elderly relatives. Official data highlights the scale of the issue, revealing that nearly eleven thousand patients waited twelve hours or more for an ambulance during August alone, though that figure was slightly lower than the previous month. Mr Anthony formally complained to the Welsh Ambulance Service and the Welsh government, describing the situation as a terrible indictment on the health service and a huge systemic problem that nobody seems to be getting to grips with.","Lee Brooks, chief operating officer for the Welsh Ambulance Service, expressed gratitude for bringing the matter to light and offered an apology, conceding that waiting almost eight hours for assistance falls far below acceptable standards. He confirmed that a preliminary review identified specific management aspects of the emergency call requiring deeper investigation to determine if staff could have responded differently. Meanwhile, the Welsh government stated that improving healthcare access remains a key priority and announced plans to release an emergency and acute care policy framework designed to enhance community response times and hospital flow. Performance figures show that while some high-priority calls meet targets, response times for orange category calls have increased significantly over recent months."],"facts":[{"fact":"A 93-year-old woman named Margaret Owen waited over 10 hours on her home floor with broken bones after falling.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Her son Graham Anthony received a lifeline alarm call at 06:15 on October 4, called an ambulance at 07:35, but help only arrived hours later.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Margaret suffered fractures to her femur and shoulder, requiring surgery, and remained in Royal Glamorgan Hospital nearly three weeks later.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Welsh Ambulance Service chief operating officer Lee Brooks apologized and stated a preliminary review is investigating how the call was managed.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Official figures show that 10,977 patients waited 12 hours or more for an ambulance in August.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"ninety-three-year-old","lemma":"ninety-three-year-old","pos":"adjective","he":"בת 93","name":false},{"text":"woman","lemma":"woman","pos":"noun","he":"אישה","name":false},{"text":"Wales","lemma":"Wales","pos":"proper noun","he":"ווילס","name":true},{"text":"suffered","lemma":"suffer","pos":"verb","he":"סבלה","name":false},{"text":"fractured","lemma":"fractured","pos":"adjective","he":"שבור","name":false},{"text":"femur","lemma":"femur","pos":"noun","he":"עצם הירך","name":false},{"text":"shoulder","lemma":"shoulder","pos":"noun","he":"כתף","name":false},{"text":"fall","lemma":"fall","pos":"noun","he":"נפילה","name":false},{"text":"home","lemma":"home","pos":"noun","he":"בית","name":false},{"text":"enduring","lemma":"endure","pos":"verb","he":"היאבקה / סבלה","name":false},{"text":"ten-and-a-half-hour","lemma":"ten-and-a-half-hour","pos":"adjective","he":"של עשר וחצי שעות","name":false},{"text":"wait","lemma":"wait","pos":"noun","he":"המתנה","name":false},{"text":"floor","lemma":"floor","pos":"noun","he":"רצפה","name":false},{"text":"ambulance","lemma":"ambulance","pos":"noun","he":"אמבולנצה","name":false},{"text":"transported","lemma":"transport","pos":"verb","he":"הובילה","name":false},{"text":"hospital","lemma":"hospital","pos":"noun","he":"בית חולים","name":false},{"text":"son","lemma":"son","pos":"noun","he":"בן","name":false},{"text":"Graham Anthony","lemma":"Graham Anthony","pos":"proper noun","he":"גרהם אנתוני","name":true},{"text":"rushed","lemma":"rush","pos":"verb","he":"מיהר","name":false},{"text":"property","lemma":"property","pos":"noun","he":"נכס / מקום מגורים","name":false},{"text":"receiving","lemma":"receive","pos":"verb","he":"קיבל","name":false},{"text":"automated","lemma":"automated","pos":"adjective","he":"מוואטט","name":false},{"text":"alert","lemma":"alert","pos":"noun","he":"התראה","name":false},{"text":"lifeline alarm","lemma":"lifeline alarm","pos":"noun","he":"אזעקת מצוקה","name":false},{"text":"early","lemma":"early","pos":"adjective","he":"מוקדם","name":false},{"text":"morning","lemma":"morning","pos":"noun","he":"בוקר","name":false},{"text":"account","lemma":"account","pos":"noun","he":"תאור / דיווח","name":false},{"text":"placed","lemma":"place","pos":"verb","he":"ביצע (שיחה)","name":false},{"text":"call","lemma":"call","pos":"noun","he":"קריאה","name":false},{"text":"shortly","lemma":"shortly","pos":"adverb","he":"מעט","name":false},{"text":"eight o'clock","lemma":"eight o'clock","pos":"noun","he":"שמונה","name":false},{"text":"yet","lemma":"yet","pos":"adverb","he":"ואף על פי כן","name":false},{"text":"professional","lemma":"professional","pos":"adjective","he":"מקצועי","name":false},{"text":"medical","lemma":"medical","pos":"adjective","he":"רפואי","name":false},{"text":"transport","lemma":"transport","pos":"noun","he":"הובלה","name":false},{"text":"arrive","lemma":"arrive","pos":"verb","he":"הגיע","name":false},{"text":"hours","lemma":"hour